As was <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/06/apple-tv-4k-four-homepods-rumor/">rumored</a> prior to today's announcements, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/new-apple-tv-4k-announced/">new Apple TV 4K</a> can connect to up to four HomePods in front-left, front-right, rear-left, and rear-right positions, enabling an all-Apple surround sound system for home theater setups.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Apple-TV-4K-Four-HomePods.jpg" alt="" width="1960" height="1102" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070548" /><br/>
You can connect four of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/apple-homepod-mini-2/">new HomePod mini 2</a> speakers to the new Apple TV 4K, or you can mix and match pairs of HomePod mini 2 and full-sized HomePod 2 speakers, so long as the front and rear pairs of speakers match. For example, you can have two full-sized HomePod 2 speakers up front and two HomePod mini 2 speakers in the rear.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is relying on computational audio. The company says the four HomePods and the new Apple TV 4K can "intelligently recognize each speaker's position in the room, so audio timing and levels are automatically calibrated to the space."<br/>
<br/>
All previous Apple TV 4K models remain limited to two HomePods for stereo sound.<br/>
<br/>
